WEBVTT

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Subhan Allah, Wa Alhamdu Lillah, Wa La Elaha Ella Allah

00:00:27.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Allahu Akbar (x4)

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:25.000
La Elaha Ella Allah

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.000
La Elaha Ella Allah.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Alhamdu Lillah, We praise God.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Wa Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.000
And we bear witness that there is no god except the one true God.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Mat was supposed to give this Khutba but he was kind enough to make an exchange with me.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.000
So, he will give the Khutba, IN SHAA ALLAH, next Friday.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.000
And I will give it today since I'll be out of town, IN SHAA ALLAH.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Also, there are some exceptional circumstances, I think,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.000
in my opinion,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:19.000
where there has been... the question has been increasingly bugging me

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:27.000
because it is, some of my best friends, some of the people that I love very much are asking the question

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.000
Why announce messengership?

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Why does Rashad say that he is messenger of God?

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.000
And I want to deal with this question.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Why can't we worship God alone and forget about messengers, and messengership and all this business?

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.000
And it is a very good question.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.000
A very important question.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.000
But I want to start out by saying that,

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.000
when you walk through this door,

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.000
you carry a great responsibility,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:08.000
you are either extremely fortunate or extremely miserable.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:15.000
And hopefully, if our destiny Inshã Allah is Heaven for worshiping God alone,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.000
we will not see any of our friends become extremely miserable.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:27.000
We have to be all, we must all catch up with being extremely fortunate.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:34.000
The Quran describes the Elite of the Elite or the extremely fortunate ones, are those who are close to Us.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.000
When you walk in this mosque and you get this message first-hand,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.000
there's a great responsibility that goes with it.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:55.000
When you walk through this door, you are applying for the highest position in the Hereafter for eternity.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:09.000
And you can just imagine the responsibility, if you think of what do we go through in this life to be an engineer or a pilot or a doctor or a lawyer.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:14.000
We have to go to school. We have to spend nights up. We have to take tests.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.000
We have to flunk a few times and struggle.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:28.000
And this is for a job that will last 20 years, will last nothing, will last zero mathematically.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.000
Cause if you compare any number divided by infinity, you have zero.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:39.000
Even if you go to this university of Arizona to get a degree to be an engineer,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.000
you get a job for a thousand years, let's say,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.000
That's zero.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:50.000
When you come here, you are applying for the best position for eternity.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.000
Therefore, the test is not easy.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.000
It is not easy to accomplish that test.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.000
I don't wanna miss anything because the question is very important.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.000
Why make the announcement that Rashad is a messenger of God?

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.000
And why dwell on it?

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Well, first of all, it's not my idea.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:22.000
As you know, I tried to evade it for eight years.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.000
because it's not easy for me either.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:29.000
And I did not make the announcement until I was fired.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:35.000
And I was scared to death. And I cried. I cried as I never did in my life.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:41.000
So, I was thrown into it, into this announcement.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:50.000
Why can't we just worship God alone and forget about the messenger and the messengership?

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.000
What's wrong with that?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:58.000
You see, belief in God implies believing God and what God says.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:05.000
If you believe in God, and you worship God alone, this means you believe everything that God says.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:10.000
And God says in the Quran, I am sending... I have angels. There are angels.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:17.000
If God says there are angels and we believe in God, then we must believe that there are angels.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.000
God says I sent down scriptures.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:26.000
And if you... if we believe in God, you believe that God sent scriptures.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.000
And God said He is sending messengers.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:34.000
Then, you must believe what God says, that He sent messengers.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.000
God said I sent Moses. Then, we must believe that.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.000
Because if we believe God, we have to believe God, what God is saying.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.000
God said I sent Jesus.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.000
This means we have to believe that Jesus is a messenger of God.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:53.000
And we see this in verse 285 of Sura 2:

00:06:53.000 --> 00:07:02.000
God says the messenger and the believers believe in God, His angels, His scriptures and His messengers.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.000
This does not violate the principle of worshiping God alone.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.000
On the contrary, it affirms it.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.000
Because, if you believe...

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:17.000
You cannot say, I'm gonna worship God alone but I don't believe everything He says.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.000
You have to believe what God says.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:35.000
God said that Muhammad was the last prophet, the last message-bearing messenger,

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.000
but not the last messenger.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.000
He said that. We have to believe that.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:46.000
In Sura 33, verse 40, and in 33:7

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.000
In 3:81, God said that after all the prophets, God will send a messenger.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:53.000
We have to believe that.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:58.000
We cannot say we're gonna worship God alone and forget about any messenger that He sends.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:02.000
In fact the verses after 81 say,

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:07.000
Anyone who does not accept this is out of the religion of Islam

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:12.000
using that word Submission, the word Islam.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.000
I want to share with you the verse 15 of Sura 49,

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:29.000
because it is very powerful and very straightforward dealing with this subject.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:34.000
Why does Rashad announce his messengership?

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.000
49:15 and 16 say:

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:45.000
that the real believers are those who believe in God and His messenger, then have no doubt.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.000
They have no doubt.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.000
And God said, بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ God and His messenger,

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Therefore, it is a tremendous test.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.000
We cannot fool God.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:07.000
If there is anything in our heart, if we are not really believers, real believers, we cannot just say it with our mouth.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:13.000
We cannot fool God. God will have to bring this out.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:17.000
And I believe this is why God forced me to make that announcement,

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.000
because some people had to be tested.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
Some people already dropped out.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:28.000
They don't deserve that high position that we are all applying for.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:32.000
Don't get me wrong though. It is perfectly alright to have doubts.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.000
But you must conquer those doubts.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:40.000
Verses 15 and 16 of Sura 49 say:

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:46.000
You are a submitter. Do not say you are a real believer, yet.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:52.000
So, this means, for as long as you are a submitter, or in Arabic, Muslim, you have doubt.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Perfectly alright.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.000
But don't let the doubts conquer you. You must conquer the doubts.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:010:00.000
Because the verse after this says:

00:010:00.000 --> 00:010:04.000
That the true believers are those who believe in God and His messenger and have no doubts.

00:010:04.000 --> 00:010:06.000
I'm gonna say it in Arabic:

00:010:06.000 --> 00:010:09.000
إِنَّمَا ٱلْمُؤْمِنُونَ The real believers

00:010:09.000 --> 00:010:14.000
ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَرْتَابُوا۟

00:010:14.000 --> 00:010:17.000
Those who believe in God and His messenger, then have no doubts.

00:010:17.000 --> 00:010:24.000
We are a family. We are one family in this mosque.

00:010:24.000 --> 00:010:27.000
There are no strangers here.

00:010:27.000 --> 00:010:37.000
We have been like this for a while because we went so fast that nobody, anybody who walks in here, they feel so much stranger. They cannot stand it.

00:010:37.000 --> 00:010:41.000
So, this is why you see the same people continuously.

00:010:41.000 --> 00:010:45.000
And until we became a family, which is in Sura 49 also.

00:010:45.000 --> 00:010:47.000
God says the believers are a family.

00:010:47.000 --> 00:010:51.000
إِنَّمَا ٱلْمُؤْمِنُونَ إِخْوَةٌۭ The believers are brothers and sisters.

00:010:51.000 --> 00:011:00.000
So we've become a family and we care. We want all of us to be at this highest position in Heaven.

00:011:00.000 --> 00:011:06.000
Because if we come this close and drop out, we're gonna be in the most pain.

00:011:06.000 --> 00:011:10.000
We're gonna be in the worst Hell in the Hereafter,

00:011:10.000 --> 00:011:16.000
And being one family, we don't want any of us to do that. We don't want this to happen to any of us.

00:011:16.000 --> 00:011:25.000
In Sura 57, I'm gonna... This is scary.

00:011:25.000 --> 00:011:34.000
Again verses 15 and 16, same verses as in Sura 49, same number of verses,

00:011:34.000 --> 00:011:49.000
It says the hypocrite men and women on that day, on the day of Judgement, will tell the people in Paradise, let us look at you so we can derive some of your light.

00:011:49.000 --> 00:011:57.000
The believers in Heaven will have the energy, the provisions,

00:011:57.000 --> 00:012:04.000
and the believers will tell them go back and get light somewhere else.

00:012:04.000 --> 00:012:11.000
Now, the scary verse is verse 14, excuse me, Sura 57, it says:

00:012:11.000 --> 00:012:17.000
They will call on them and say, were we not with you? We were with you.

00:012:17.000 --> 00:012:23.000
The hypocrite men and women will say to the believers, we were with you. Were we not with you?

00:012:23.000 --> 00:012:26.000
أَلَم نَكُن مَعَكُم in Arabic. Were we not with you?

00:012:26.000 --> 00:012:35.000
And the believers will say yes, but you deceived yourselves,

00:012:35.000 --> 00:012:42.000
waited, you know, dillydallied, in the colloquial English, dillydally around,

00:012:42.000 --> 00:012:46.000
And you had doubts,

00:012:46.000 --> 00:012:52.000
and you were deceived by wishful thinking, until God's command came.

00:012:52.000 --> 00:013:03.000
OK. So, can this happen to us? I mean, It has to happen, it has to happen to... to... in connection with us,

00:013:03.000 --> 00:013:06.000
We're going to grow in the future.

00:013:06.000 --> 00:013:10.000
And there will be hypocrite men and women who will come here, who'll be with us.

00:013:10.000 --> 00:013:14.000
And they will ask this question on the Day of Judgment and eternity. They will say were we not with you?

00:013:14.000 --> 00:013:20.000
We came to the Quranic study with you. We came to the Friday prayer with you. We sat with you and we were friends.

00:013:20.000 --> 00:013:25.000
And the believers will say yes, but you had doubts.

00:013:25.000 --> 00:013:28.000
Therefore, you must work on your doubts,

00:013:28.000 --> 00:013:31.000
and you must conquer those doubts.

00:013:31.000 --> 00:013:35.000
And God made it connected with God and His messenger.

00:013:35.000 --> 00:013:38.000
And I learn from this, why the announcement.

00:013:38.000 --> 00:013:42.000
I have seen the people who dropped out

00:013:42.000 --> 00:013:47.000
And they were invariably the people that I have known all along that they don't belong.

00:013:47.000 --> 00:013:56.000
And when the announcement came, the sifting process started which is very necessary.

00:013:56.000 --> 00:014:03.000
Why can't we just believe in God alone, worship God alone and forget about the message, the messenger, or everything else? God alone.

00:014:03.000 --> 00:014:08.000
Satan can deceive you through that statement.

00:014:08.000 --> 00:014:16.000
We must be wise because worshiping God alone implies believing everything God says.

00:014:16.000 --> 00:014:22.000
And God says very clearly certain statements including:

00:014:22.000 --> 00:014:27.000
that Muhammad would be the last prophet but not the last messenger,

00:014:27.000 --> 00:014:30.000
that a messenger comes after all the prophets,

00:014:30.000 --> 00:014:36.000
a consolidating messenger who will put the messages all together into one, present it to the world.

00:014:36.000 --> 00:014:39.000
The Messenger of the Covenant.

00:014:39.000 --> 00:014:44.000
And the verses after the Messenger of the Covenant are very strong and saying:

00:014:44.000 --> 00:014:47.000
Those who do not believe this are out of Islam.

00:014:47.000 --> 00:014:49.000
God is saying all this.

00:014:49.000 --> 00:014:53.000
and God spelled the name of the Messenger of the Covenant, Rashad Khalifa.

00:014:53.000 --> 00:014:54.000
God spelled it in the Quran.

00:014:54.000 --> 00:014:58.000
And if we are to worship God alone, we have to believe what God said.

00:015:01.000 --> 00:015:04.000
Edip and I were talking yesterday on the index to the Quran,

00:015:04.000 --> 00:015:10.000
which ironically was published, printed and published, one year before I was born,

00:015:10.000 --> 00:015:14.000
and in it, the root word Rashada is 19 times.

00:015:14.000 --> 00:015:17.000
And I thank God that I didn't discover that.

00:015:17.000 --> 00:015:19.000
It wasn't me. It was Edip actually who discovered it.

00:015:19.000 --> 00:015:21.000
First person ever.

00:015:21.000 --> 00:015:26.000
And if you remember the Khutba, those of you, the old timers, remember the Khutba that I gave about that.

00:015:26.000 --> 00:015:30.000
And I was thankful that I didn't discover it. I was afraid of my ego.

00:015:30.000 --> 00:015:36.000
that I may say, it's my ego, I was looking for it. I didn't even look for... I was afraid to look for that.

00:015:36.000 --> 00:015:41.000
So, it came from the other side of the globe.

00:015:46.000 --> 00:015:50.000
If we want to worship God alone, we must believe everything God says.

00:015:50.000 --> 00:015:52.000
Tooboo Ela Allah. Repent

00:016:09.000 --> 00:016:11.000
Alhamdu Lillah. We praise God

00:016:11.000 --> 00:016:14.000
Wa Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah.

00:016:14.000 --> 00:016:19.000
I'm gonna borrow this example from Edip again.

00:016:19.000 --> 00:016:27.000
If you get ill and you go to somebody and he says take these pills.

00:016:27.000 --> 00:016:32.000
and you take the pills and you're healed,

00:016:32.000 --> 00:016:38.000
and this happens again two or three times and every time he gives you some medicine, you're healed.

00:016:38.000 --> 00:016:43.000
Then, you will make a conclusion saying this person knows medicine.

00:016:43.000 --> 00:016:47.000
You're gonna have doubts for some time.

00:016:47.000 --> 00:016:54.000
You're not sure if he is a witch doctor or a real doctor or is it coincidence or what.

00:016:54.000 --> 00:017:04.000
But if he is a certified doctor and he gives you the medicine, then, you'll have... you'll trust this person.

00:017:04.000 --> 00:017:06.000
You don't have these doubts anymore.

00:017:06.000 --> 00:017:11.000
And this is why God ordered the announcement.

00:017:14.000 --> 00:017:20.000
It was... I was... I was promoting this opinion let's worship God alone.

00:017:20.000 --> 00:017:24.000
Spread the word in the world that we're gonna follow the word of God alone, the Quran alone and worship God alone.

00:017:24.000 --> 00:017:27.000
Why? Why the announcement?

00:017:27.000 --> 00:017:29.000
I actually believed this for a long time.

00:017:29.000 --> 00:017:36.000
And I remember I was talking with Ismail Barakat

00:017:36.000 --> 00:017:42.000
Some of you who participated in the noise of the first conference in San Francisco,

00:017:42.000 --> 00:017:46.000
and Ismail was very angry,

00:017:46.000 --> 00:017:52.000
and he determined to ask me, point-blank, are you a messenger of God?

00:017:52.000 --> 00:018:00.000
Now for eight years, I was praying to God that nobody would ask me that question, point-blank.

00:018:00.000 --> 00:018:05.000
Some people did ask me Are you a prophet? And I said Muhammad is the last prophet.

00:018:05.000 --> 00:018:09.000
I was very clever and I avoided that for a long time.

00:018:09.000 --> 00:018:13.000
And I was praying that nobody would ask me the question.

00:018:13.000 --> 00:018:15.000
Now, when that noise happened in San Francisco,

00:018:15.000 --> 00:018:20.000
and Ismail, he's gonna be here in a week or two. He's getting here very soon,

00:018:20.000 --> 00:018:22.000
I'm gonna ask him to tell you that story

00:018:22.000 --> 00:018:30.000
because he swears that he was determined to ask me, point-blank, are you a messenger of God? in San Francisco.

00:018:30.000 --> 00:018:34.000
And when that noise happened, I prayed very hard, as I never prayed before.

00:018:34.000 --> 00:018:37.000
Please God, don't let anybody ask me that question

00:018:37.000 --> 00:018:42.000
Because Susan Ray, if you remember, made an announcement and said Rashad Khalifa is a messenger of God.

00:018:42.000 --> 00:018:44.000
I wasn't ready for it.

00:018:44.000 --> 00:018:46.000
And I prayed very hard.

00:018:46.000 --> 00:018:52.000
And Ismail until today would say I don't know how it happened, but I didn't ask that question.

00:018:52.000 --> 00:018:55.000
So, I guess my prayer was stronger than his determination.

00:018:57.000 --> 00:019:02.000
Because I wouldn't, I would have told him yes at the time.

00:019:02.000 --> 00:019:04.000
Because I knew it for eight years.

00:019:04.000 --> 00:019:08.000
And I evaded it for eight years. It was not my idea.

00:019:08.000 --> 00:019:13.000
So, why? why would anybody...

00:019:13.000 --> 00:019:18.000
I want to deal in this Khutba with the question how to overcome the doubts?

00:019:18.000 --> 00:019:23.000
So, don't let me finish without answering the question. How can you overcome that doubt?

00:019:23.000 --> 00:019:36.000
But before I say that, I want to explain why does the person flunk and drop out if he does not believe that Rashad Khalifa is God's messenger of the Covenant,

00:019:36.000 --> 00:019:42.000
Or if he is annoyed by this repetition or dwelling on it.

00:019:42.000 --> 00:019:46.000
It is not a fact in his or her mind.

00:019:46.000 --> 00:019:49.000
And the answer is in Sura 45, verse 23

00:019:49.000 --> 00:019:54.000
which tells us the last god that we may have besides God.

00:019:54.000 --> 00:019:58.000
It says: Have you seen the one whose god is his ego?

00:019:58.000 --> 00:020:01.000
his or her ego.

00:020:01.000 --> 00:020:08.000
If God is saying there is a messenger after Muhammad, what does he look like? What is his qualifications?

00:020:08.000 --> 00:020:10.000
What are his qualifications?

00:020:10.000 --> 00:020:13.000
Is he gonna be somebody with wings?

00:020:13.000 --> 00:020:17.000
A strange-looking person or what?

00:020:17.000 --> 00:020:20.000
Is he gonna be a human being like us? one like us?

00:020:20.000 --> 00:020:22.000
Maybe even a silly one.

00:020:22.000 --> 00:020:28.000
Why are you laughing?

00:020:28.000 --> 00:020:30.000
What will he look like?

00:020:30.000 --> 00:020:33.000
So, why then should we not believe God?

00:020:33.000 --> 00:020:39.000
when He's telling all these things and spelling the name in the Quran.

00:020:39.000 --> 00:020:41.000
If you read appendix two of the new translation,

00:020:41.000 --> 00:020:47.000
you'll see how much evidence there is. God is not subtle. God is not subtle.

00:020:47.000 --> 00:020:52.000
God's evidence is so powerful, it's not even funny. It's so overwhelming.

00:020:52.000 --> 00:020:56.000
So, this helps the believers remove all doubt,

00:020:56.000 --> 00:021:00.000
but the ego would be the only thing.

